{#- The coil selection calculator: four small tools that share one unit system,
    written by hand rather than published from SpreadsheetConverter. The maths is
    in /assets/js/coil.js, which check-calculators.mjs holds to the workbook's own
    answers; this is only the form. It never submits. -#}
{%- macro solveFor(name, opts) %}
<div class="field"><label for="co-{{ name }}">Solve for</label>
  <select id="co-{{ name }}" name="{{ name }}">{% for o in opts %}<option value="{{ o[0] }}">{{ o[1] }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div>
{%- endmacro %}
{%- macro num(id, label, unitClass, unit, eg) %}
<div class="field co-f" data-var="{{ id }}"><label for="co-{{ id }}">{{ label }} <span class="cf-u {{ unitClass }}">{{ unit }}</span></label>
  <input type="number" id="co-{{ id }}" name="{{ id }}" inputmode="decimal" step="any" autocomplete="off" placeholder="{{ eg }}"></div>
{%- endmacro %}
<form class="calcform" id="cocalc" novalidate>
  <noscript><p class="cf-noscript">This calculator runs in your browser and needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  <div class="cf-inputs">
    <fieldset class="cf-radios">
      <legend>Units (all tools)</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="u" value="English" checked> US</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="u" value="Metric"> Metric</label>
    </fieldset>

    {#- One tool at a time: the buttons show that tool's inputs and results. The
        others keep their entries, so the links between tools still work. #}
    <fieldset class="co-pick">
      <legend>Tool</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="tool" value="air" checked> 1. Air side</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="tool" value="face"> 2. Face velocity</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="tool" value="water"> 3. Fluid flow</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="tool" value="tubes"> 4. Tube velocity</label>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="cf-stream co-tool" data-tool="air">
      <legend>1. Coil air side: entering and leaving air, airflow, and sensible, latent and total cooling</legend>
      {#- Optional: naming the answer hides its inputs, so what is typed there
          cannot over-define it. "Whatever" leaves every input open. #}
      <div class="co-solve">{{ solveFor("as", [["any", "Whatever the entries allow"], ["loads", "Coil loads"], ["airflow", "Airflow"], ["leaving", "Leaving air"], ["entering", "Entering air"]]) }}</div>
      {%- set moisture = [["db-wb", "Wet bulb"], ["db-rh", "Rel. hum."], ["db-dp", "Dew point"]] %}
      {#- The moisture of one end: how it is known, and its value, on one line. -#}
      {%- macro moist(sel, id, which, unitClass, eg) %}
        <div class="field co-f" data-var="{{ id }}"><label for="co-{{ id }}">{{ which }} air moisture <span class="cf-u {{ unitClass }}">°F</span></label>
          <div class="co-moist"><select id="co-{{ sel }}" name="{{ sel }}" aria-label="{{ which }} air moisture given as">{% for o in moisture %}<option value="{{ o[0] }}">{{ o[1] }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>
          <input type="number" id="co-{{ id }}" name="{{ id }}" inputmode="decimal" step="any" autocomplete="off" placeholder="{{ eg }}"></div></div>
      {%- endmacro %}
      <div class="cf-pair">{{ num("e1", "Entering dry bulb", "co-t", "°F", "80") }}{{ num("x1", "Leaving dry bulb", "co-t", "°F", "55") }}</div>
      <div class="cf-pair">{{ moist("am1", "e2", "Entering", "co-m1", "67") }}{{ moist("am2", "x2", "Leaving", "co-m2", "54") }}</div>
      {{ num("aq", "Airflow", "co-a", "cfm", "1000") }}
      <div class="cf-trio co-loads">{{ num("qs", "Sensible cooling", "co-q", "Btu/h", "27000") }}{{ num("ql", "Latent cooling", "co-q", "Btu/h", "9000") }}{{ num("qt", "Total cooling", "co-q", "Btu/h", "36000") }}</div>
      <p class="hint cf-group">Coil loads, not room loads: include the outdoor air and fan heat. A room load from a load calculation is usually smaller.</p>
      <p class="hint cf-group co-next" id="co-loadhint" role="status" hidden></p>
      {{ num("alt", "Altitude", "co-l", "ft", "0") }}
      <p class="hint cf-group">Fill in any of the inputs; results appear as soon as there are enough to work with.
      Not sure which inputs you need? Ask the help chat in the bottom right corner.</p>
      <details class="cf-howto">
      <summary>More detail</summary>
      <p class="hint">Enter what you know and leave the rest blank. Solve for is optional: choosing an answer hides its inputs.
      Both air conditions and the airflow give the sensible, latent and total cooling. Both air conditions
      and one coil load give the airflow. One air condition, the airflow and any two of the three coil loads give the
      air at the other end, as do the total cooling and that end's RH or dew point. Less than that still
      gives part of the answer: the dry bulbs alone give the sensible cooling, and dew points alone the latent.
      If you enter more than is needed, a note under the results says which entry was not used. Each air state
      comes from its dry bulb and wet bulb, RH or dew point, with the ASHRAE psychrometric equations at the
      altitude given (sea level if blank). The airflow is at the entering air; the same airflow is used for
      the coil face velocity below. Entering air is the air at the coil: return or mixed air for a
      recirculating system, outdoor air for a DOAS.</p>
      </details>
    </fieldset>

    {#- From tool 1, the tools it feeds can be opened under it, each once tool 1
        has the value it needs. The ticks are saved through the hidden "adds"
        field, so a shared link opens the same tools. #}
    <div class="co-adds" id="co-adds" hidden>
      <span class="co-adds-h">Continue with:</span>
      <label data-add="face" hidden><input type="checkbox" value="face"> Face velocity</label>
      <label data-add="water" hidden><input type="checkbox" value="water"> Fluid flow</label>
      <label data-add="tubes" hidden><input type="checkbox" value="tubes"> Tube velocity</label>
      <input type="text" name="adds" id="co-adds-v" value="" hidden>
    </div>

    <fieldset class="cf-stream co-tool" data-tool="face">
      <legend>2. Coil face area and velocity</legend>
      <div class="cf-pair">{{ num("fh", "Face height", "co-d", "in", "24") }}{{ num("fw", "Face width", "co-d", "in", "36") }}</div>
      {{ num("fq", "Airflow", "co-a", "cfm", "1000") }}
      <p class="hint">The same airflow as tool 1: typing it in either place fills in both, and a blank box takes the airflow tool 1 finds.</p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="cf-stream co-tool" data-tool="water">
      <legend>3. Fluid flow (water or glycol)</legend>
      {{ solveFor("wf", [["load", "Coil load"], ["flow", "Flow rate"], ["entering", "Entering temperature"], ["leaving", "Leaving temperature"]]) }}
      <div class="field"><label for="co-fluid">Fluid</label>
        <select id="co-fluid" name="fl">{% for f in ["Water", "Ethylene Glycol 10%", "Ethylene Glycol 20%", "Ethylene Glycol 30%", "Ethylene Glycol 40%", "Ethylene Glycol 50%", "Propylene Glycol 10%", "Propylene Glycol 20%", "Propylene Glycol 30%", "Propylene Glycol 40%", "Propylene Glycol 50%"] %}<option value="{{ f }}">{{ f }}{% if "Glycol" in f %} (by volume){% endif %}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div>
      <fieldset class="cf-radios">
        <legend>Coil</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name="wc" value="Cooling" checked> Cooling (fluid warms up)</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="wc" value="Heating"> Heating (fluid cools down)</label>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="cf-pair">{{ num("w1", "Entering fluid", "co-t", "°F", "45") }}{{ num("w2", "Leaving fluid", "co-t", "°F", "55") }}</div>
      <div class="cf-pair">{{ num("w3", "Coil load", "co-q", "Btu/h", "240000") }}{{ num("w4", "Flow rate", "co-g", "gpm", "48") }}</div>
      <p class="hint" id="co-w3-hint">Leave the coil load blank to use the total cooling from tool 1.</p>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="cf-stream co-tool" data-tool="tubes">
      <legend>4. Fluid velocity in coil tubes</legend>
      <div class="cf-trio">{{ num("vq", "Flow rate", "co-g", "gpm", "48") }}{{ num("vd", "Tube inside dia.", "co-td", "in", "0.5") }}{{ num("vn", "Tubes fed", "", "", "12") }}</div>
      <p class="hint">Leave the flow rate blank to use the flow from tool 3.</p>
    </fieldset>

    <p class="cf-actions">
      <button type="reset" class="btn btn-quiet">Reset</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-quiet" id="co-share" hidden>Copy link to these results</button>
      <span class="cf-copied" id="co-copied" role="status"></span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="cf-results" aria-labelledby="co-results-h">
    <h2 id="co-results-h">Results</h2>
    <p class="cf-summary" id="co-summary" role="status">Fill in any of the tools; each result appears as soon as its inputs are complete.</p>
    {#- For each tool, what it needs for each answer, shown until it has one.
        Picking an answer rings the inputs it needs until that answer appears;
        in the fluid tool it also sets Solve for. -#}
    <div class="co-guide" data-tool="air" hidden>
      <p class="co-guide-h">What do you want to calculate? Pick one to highlight the inputs it needs.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="e1 e2 x1 x2 aq" data-done="Total cooling" data-as="loads" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the sensible, latent and total cooling:</strong> enter the entering air, the leaving air and the airflow.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="e1 e2 x1 x2 qs ql qt" data-done="Airflow" data-as="airflow" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the airflow:</strong> enter the entering air, the leaving air and one of the three coil loads.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="e1 e2 aq qs ql qt" data-done="Leaving wet bulb" data-as="leaving" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the leaving air:</strong> enter the entering air, the airflow and two of the three coil loads (or the total cooling and the leaving RH or dew point).</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="x1 x2 aq qs ql qt" data-done="Entering wet bulb" data-as="entering" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the entering air:</strong> enter the leaving air, the airflow and two of the three coil loads (or the total cooling and the entering RH or dew point).</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="e1 x1 aq" data-done="Sensible cooling" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the sensible cooling alone:</strong> enter the two dry bulbs and the airflow.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="e2 x2 aq" data-done="Latent cooling" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the latent cooling alone:</strong> enter the two dew points and the airflow.</button></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Picking one also sets Solve for. The entering or leaving air means its dry bulb plus a wet bulb, RH or dew point.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="co-guide" data-tool="face" hidden>
      <p class="co-guide-h">What do you want to calculate? Pick one to highlight the inputs it needs.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="fh fw" data-done="Coil face area" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the coil face area:</strong> enter the face height and width.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="fh fw fq" data-done="Coil face velocity" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the face velocity:</strong> enter the face height and width and the airflow (or leave the airflow blank to use the one tool 1 finds).</button></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Face velocity is the airflow divided by the face area.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="co-guide" data-tool="water" hidden>
      <p class="co-guide-h">What do you want to calculate? Pick one to highlight the inputs it needs.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="w1 w2 w3" data-done="Fluid flow rate" data-solve="flow" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the fluid flow rate:</strong> enter the entering and leaving fluid temperatures and the coil load (or leave the coil load blank to use the total cooling from tool 1).</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="w1 w2 w4" data-done="Coil load" data-solve="load" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the coil load:</strong> enter the entering and leaving fluid temperatures and the flow rate.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="w2 w3 w4" data-done="Entering fluid" data-solve="entering" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the entering fluid temperature:</strong> enter the leaving fluid temperature, the coil load and the flow rate.</button></li>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="w1 w3 w4" data-done="Leaving fluid" data-solve="leaving" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the leaving fluid temperature:</strong> enter the entering fluid temperature, the coil load and the flow rate.</button></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Picking one also sets Solve for. Choose the fluid and whether the coil is cooling or heating first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="co-guide" data-tool="tubes" hidden>
      <p class="co-guide-h">What do you want to calculate? Pick one to highlight the inputs it needs.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><button type="button" class="co-target" data-need="vq vd vn" data-done="Fluid velocity in tubes" aria-pressed="false"><strong>To calculate the fluid velocity in the tubes:</strong> enter the flow rate (or leave it blank to use the flow from tool 3), the tube inside diameter and the number of tubes fed.</button></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Tube velocity is the flow divided by the total inside area of the tubes fed.</p>
    </div>
    <table class="cf-table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Results of each tool</caption><tbody id="co-tbody"></tbody></table>
    <p class="cf-note" id="co-note" hidden></p>
  </section>
</form>
